codex
The package confirms the default live contest shape in the CLI is width 256, depth 32, 10 MLPs, FLOP budget `272e9`, and `2,560,000` target samples. I’ll use that as the likely blackbox configuration while keeping the code adaptive.
codex
A promising change is to keep an approximate mean/covariance model after layer 2 and use it to calibrate later Monte Carlo preactivations. Before editing, I’ll quickly check which special functions `flopscope.numpy` exposes for Gaussian moment formulas.
